🧠 Conclusions

K-Means is effective for clearly separated clusters but merges overlapping classes.
DBSCAN identifies noise well but requires careful parameter tuning; performance is sensitive to eps and minPts.
Anomaly Detection shows consistent results across KNN, LOF, and Isolation Forest, particularly flagging Virginica as more variable or noisy.
Combining multiple unsupervised methods provides a robust view of the underlying data structure, helping validate both clusters and outliers.